<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Stuff-first hauling and loading - dnbl-architecture.md section 18.
  Vanilla XML patch (not Harmony) adding DNBL's own cargo-protection comp
  to every humanlike pawn ThingDef, the same mechanism Pick Up And Haul
  uses for its CompHauledToInventory (Patches/PickUpAndHaul.xml in its own
  mod folder, read for inspiration only - no PUAH type or file referenced
  here).

  Narrowed 2026-09-22 to colonists only, on the user's order. "Colonist"
  is a runtime fact (faction, slave/guest status) that no ThingDef can
  express, so this xpath only narrows as far as a ThingDef can: humanlike
  race, which drops every animal and mechanoid ThingDef. The remaining
  runtime narrowing - player faction, not a raider or prisoner - is done
  in CompDnblCargo itself. race/intelligence="Humanlike" (not a hardcoded
  defName="Human") so a modded humanlike race keeps working; verified
  against lib\Assembly-CSharp.dll that ThingDef's race field is
  Verse.RaceProperties with a public field named intelligence of enum
  Verse.Intelligence (Animal, ToolUser, Humanlike), defaulting to Animal,
  so any def actually meaning to be humanlike must write it out in XML.
-->
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[thingClass="Pawn" and race/intelligence="Humanlike"]/comps</xpath>
		<value>
			<li Class="DoNotBeLazy.Comps.CompProperties_DnblCargo" />
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
